# Phase 3 parity continuation — 2026-09-26T15:15:00Z

- Continued from clean baseline commit `74f3274`; strict Java 5.5.1 parity remains the target. Phase 3 remains unaccepted, Phase 4 not started, and plans were not changed.
- Audited `Connection::encode_command`, `send`, `try_send`, `run_connection`, and `OutboundFrame::drop` to trace frame ownership/recycling through encode failure, queue admission timeout/rejection/closed queue, write error, caller cancellation, and connection shutdown. Added explicit pool-content assertions for encode failure, queue admission timeout, write error, cancellation and shutdown; retained existing success/rejection/four-buffer-bound coverage. No pool implementation behavior change was needed; the ownership guard/drop already recycles these buffers.
- Tightened SOCKS route unit-test determinism: Java-compatible route selection iterates a HashMap with unspecified order, so a test combining a specific CIDR and default route could nondeterministically select the default first. Separate assertions now isolate specific-route and default-route matching; implementation semantics unchanged.
- Updated `docs/compatibility/PHASE_3_REMOTING_INVENTORY.md` to list the new individual allocator lifecycle test coverage, without claiming Netty allocator parity.
- Validation passed: `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked --offline -- -D warnings`; `cargo test --workspace --locked --offline` (common 11, protocol 9+1 integration, remoting 27 unit + 4 codec + 63 transport); `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; `git diff --check`.
- No Java Maven, Broker, Docker or cross-language live validation performed. Outstanding documented blockers include actual Netty channel/context/event-loop semantics, executor ownership/shutdown/thread lifecycle, TLS global reload lifecycle, exception/cause parity and scheduling/race parity. `P3-V04` remains Phase 19. This batch does not complete or accept Phase 3.
- Pending commit at log creation; final status/commit to be added only in a later append-only log entry if needed (do not edit this log).
